---
/**
 * Fender Mustang dating guide. SEVENTH OF THE MODEL-AXIS SPOKES.
 *
 * Sibling of the Stratocaster, Telecaster, Jazzmaster, Jaguar, Jazz Bass and
 * Precision Bass dating guides. Built on joe/mustang-dating-spoke, stacked on
 * joe/precision-bass-dating-spoke.
 *
 * WHAT MAKES THE MUSTANG PAGE DIFFERENT. Do not clone the other six:
 *   - THE MUSTANG ARRIVED IN 1964, AFTER MOST OF THE TELLS. Slab boards ended
 *     mid-1962, the spaghetti logo era had closed, and clay dots were nearly
 *     out. So the standard pre-CBS checklist a reader brings from a Strat or a
 *     Tele mostly does not apply here, and several of its items are red flags
 *     rather than dates. That absence is the page's spine and it comes right
 *     after the three passes.
 *   - WHAT DATES IT INSTEAD IS MUSTANG-ONLY HARDWARE. The Dynamic Vibrato was
 *     built for this model and appears on no other vintage Fender, and the word
 *     engraved on it ("Pat. Pend." versus a patent number) splits 1964-66 from
 *     1967 on. No other model page can use a part that exists nowhere else.
 *   - THE COMPETITION FINISHES ARE A SECOND, PARALLEL DATING AXIS, in four
 *     steps (wrap-around stripes, matching painted headstock, front-only
 *     stripes plus natural headstock, then gone). No sibling page has a
 *     sub-series that dates itself.
 *   - THE PICKGUARD COLOUR IS PAIRED TO THE BODY COLOUR, which makes guard
 *     versus finish an originality check rather than a date. Jazzmaster
 *     territory in spirit, but the pairing rule itself is Mustang-specific.
 *
 * CONTRAST WITH THE JAGUAR, STATED BRIEFLY AND NOT EXPANDED: on a Jaguar the
 * logo does not date the guitar. On a Mustang it does, in two steps. The Jaguar
 * page owns the logo-trap framing; this page states the inversion in one line
 * and cross-references, the same way the Jazz Bass page does.
 *
 * JOE'S REVIEW RULES, carried over from the six sibling pages:
 *   - Features give a WINDOW. Only the neck heel date and the body date give a
 *     month.
 *   - The serial belongs in the second pass, read as one vote among several.
 *   - Never call a feature "model-specific" without checking it.
 *   - Never say "bare wood" about a body date.
 *   - Keep a photo caption on the one thing the photo is for.
 *
 * FACT SOURCING. Every dated claim traces to the Mustang fact set added to
 * joes-vintage-databases as VG-0147 to VG-0161. Numbered from 0147 because main
 * is at VG-0117 and the open PRs already claim 0113-0114 (#1/#2, an unresolved
 * collision), 0118-0130 (#4, Jazz Bass) and 0131-0146 (#5, Precision Bass).
 * Before this set there were ZERO Mustang entries in the registry.
 *
 * CONTRADICTION IN THE SOURCE, flagged to Joe and NOT propagated. The live
 * Mustang guide dates the wrap-around Competition stripe two different ways:
 * its year table puts front-only stripes at 1970 to 1971 ("Competition finishes
 * continue, now stripes on the front only"), while its Competition section says
 * "the earliest 1968 examples had stripes that wrapped around the body, while
 * from late 1968 on the stripes are on the front only." This page follows the
 * Competition section, which is the more specific of the two, and treats the
 * wrap-around as a 1968-only feature.
 *
 * NO YEAR-TO-SERIAL-NUMBER TABLE, same as the six sibling pages. The Mustang
 * guide itself carries an F-plate range table; that belongs to the hub, where
 * the charts live once, and VG-0066..0068 are KEEP FLAGGED on numeric ranges.
 *
 * VOICE. Written against the 2026-08-11 VOICE_GUIDE additions: No Self-Ranked
 * Importance (no sentence whose only job is to say something matters, no
 * "worth knowing" preambles, no "the single most X") and Do Not Repeat A
 * Section Template (every heading names its own content; none repeats).
 */
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import LicensedImage from "../components/primitives/LicensedImage.astro";
import { resolveImage, assetSrc, ogCardSize } from "../lib/images";
import { contact, hrefs, SITE_URL } from "../config/site";

const meta = (file: string) => resolveImage("images/fender-sn/" + file)!;
